! C2H7O3Cl | wB97X-D/PCseg-2/PCM(water) -- native basis, sidesteps DGEMM bug
!
! ============================================================
! Why this file exists
! ============================================================
! caa005bIRCCML1stdef2TZVPPe.inp (wB97X-D/def2-TZVPP/PCM(water), starting
! from the confirmed 6-31G(d,p) minimum) showed 16 simultaneous negative
! Hessian eigenvalues purely from enlarging the basis -- reproducing
! closely across two independently computed Hessians. Separately, we spent
! considerable effort chasing a "DGEMM parameter 13 illegal value" crash
! affecting ANY custom-supplied basis (both BASNAM and EXTFIL mechanisms)
! below a certain size on this specific ARCHER2 GAMESS build -- confirmed
! NOT to affect GAMESS's own built-in GBASIS-driven basis construction
! (validated via the full 49-test bundled example suite).
!
! A GAMESS Google Group response (from a related but different thread)
! suggested trying the PCseg family (Jensen's Polarization Consistent
! segmented basis sets) as an alternative to cc-pVTZ/def2-TZVPP-style
! bases, specifically raising the possibility that the CONSTRUCTION of
! those basis families could itself be contributing to linear-dependence-
! type problems, and that a newer basis family might behave better.
! PCseg-2 is roughly equivalent in quality to cc-pVTZ (~TZ2P).
!
! This is a genuinely attractive test for two independent reasons:
! 1. It directly tests the forum's scientific hypothesis (does a
!    differently-constructed triple-zeta-quality basis show the same
!    instability at this geometry?).
! 2. PCseg-2 is NATIVELY supported by GAMESS via plain GBASIS=PCSEG-2 --
!    no BASNAM, no EXTFIL, no custom basis blocks at all. This completely
!    sidesteps the DGEMM crash rather than working around it, since we
!    have direct evidence (the 49-test suite) that built-in GBASIS
!    construction is unaffected by that bug.
!
! IMPORTANT, confirmed directly from this GAMESS version's own docs-input.txt:
! the PCseg family REQUIRES spherical harmonics (ISPHER=1 in $CONTRL) --
! "The calculations will refuse to run without ISPHER being set." This is
! mandatory, not a style choice.
!
! Starting geometry: the confirmed genuine minimum from
! caa005bIRCCML1st-prerelax-631Gdp.inp (wB97X-D/6-31G(d,p)/PCM(water),
! EXECUTION OF GAMESS TERMINATED NORMALLY, zero imaginary frequencies).
!
! Optimizer settings otherwise identical to caa005bIRCCML1stdef2TZVPPd/e.inp
! (conservative DXMAX=0.01, IHREP=2, METHOD=SEMINUM since wB97X-D has no
! analytic Hessian regardless of basis, Cartesian coordinates, SOSCF,
! DIRSCF) so that basis choice is the only variable changed relative to
! those runs.

 $CONTRL SCFTYP=RHF RUNTYP=OPTIMIZE DFTTYP=wB97X-D
         COORD=UNIQUE MAXIT=200 NOSYM=1 ISPHER=1
 $END
 $GUESS GUESS=HUCKEL $END
 $BASIS GBASIS=PCSEG-2 $END
 $SCF CONV=1.0D-6
     SOSCF=.T.
     DAMP=.F.
     SHIFT=.T.
     DIRSCF=.TRUE.
 $END
 $STATPT OPTTOL=0.0001 NSTEP=300 IHREP=2 HSSEND=.T. DXMAX=0.01 NPRT=1 $END
 $ZMAT DLC=.F. AUTO=.F. $END
 $FORCE METHOD=SEMINUM PROJCT=.T. $END
 $PCM SOLVNT=WATER $END
 $SYSTEM MWORDS=100 MEMDDI=200 $END

 $DATA
Chloroacetaldehyde hydrate and water -- wB97X-D/PCseg-2/PCM(water)
C1
Cl   17.0   3.4062263771   0.2091279057   0.2533561081
C     6.0   2.2845933847   0.8634093872  -0.9829615815
C     6.0   2.9679220138   1.8831295208  -1.8632833921
O     8.0   2.3265477065   2.6992356036  -2.4903771140
H     1.0   1.4219922861   1.3024323058  -0.4827108444
H     1.0   1.9669509886   0.0324484665  -1.6146227258
O     8.0   3.5738284953   0.0679565750  -3.8462810595
O     8.0   3.9842881842   2.6765444468  -4.8076254061
H     1.0   3.5078817045   2.7937321447  -5.6358114425
H     1.0   3.7893562925   0.9104597543  -4.2899067776
H     1.0   2.7388546345  -0.1945985132  -4.2445882765
